> I found two critical issues
> 
> 1. If the Cyclic mode includes anything other than NodeAnimation, it should not be processed in the first place. Since extra case statements are required for items that cannot be processed correctly, the entire process should be aborted
> 2. Discrete mode is not supported correctly
> 
> I’ve uploaded a patch that addresses these issues partially. Regarding Discrete mode, I’ve only fixed BlendSpace2D, so after applying the patch, please apply the fix to BlendSpace1D as well.
> 
> [0001-Refactor-blending-code-modify-warning-on-BSEditor.patch](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25990117/0001-Refactor-blending-code-modify-warning-on-BSEditor.patch)
> 
> Also, I’ve made the following changes to the GUI. Simply displaying “No sync” isn’t very helpful because it doesn’t convey the reason to the user. Instead, it should indicate that the point itself is invalid and completely abort the process. I have commented out the implementation for the error popup as a TODO, so please implement that.
> 
> <img alt="Image" width="384" height="180" src="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/61938263/563401959-bafce6d8-9661-4daf-bbe6-c8d8d3b2a479.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..mAuxyIuCTMXsLU31CeR6YLXkIS-kqHuBIJqzkGehXPQ">
> Furthermore, your current implementation handles seek operations, but I believe we need to test it a bit more to ensure it works correctly. Since your current code is inconsistent with the TimeScale node, if you plan to support seek, I think you should submit a separate follow-up PR to implement additional options alongside NodeTimeScale, rather than including it in this PR.

While putting in your patch I noticed something that can result in issues with the method your suggesting.

`triangle_points` is only populated in interpolated mode. In discrete mode it stays zero-initialized (`{0, 0, 0}`), so this loop only ever checks/sets `deltas[0]`. If `new_closest > 0`, no point receives a delta — all remain `-1`, `signbit()` skips everything, and the closest animation never gets blended.

The discrete carry path doesn't rescue this because it only fires on transitions (`new_closest != cur_closest`). Once settled on a point, steady-state playback freezes.

The 1D version handles this correctly by iterating `blend_points_used`:

```cpp
} else {
    for (int i = 0; i < blend_points_used; i++) {
        if (weights[i] >= CMP_EPSILON) {
            deltas[i] = pi.delta;
        }
    }
}
